---

<TourPageLayout
  tour={tour}
  title="Day Trips From Nairobi | Naivasha, Hell's Gate, Nakuru & Amboseli"
  description="Private day trips from Nairobi to Lake Naivasha, Hell's Gate, Lake Nakuru, Mount Longonot and Amboseli. Early pick-up, back in the city the same evening."
  h1="Day trips from Nairobi"
  lede="A day trip from Nairobi is a single-day guided excursion out of the city and back the same evening, most often to Lake Naivasha, Hell&rsquo;s Gate National Park, Lake Nakuru, Mount Longonot, the Ngong Hills or Amboseli. Nairobi Adventures runs these as private trips with an early start, because the driving is what makes or breaks a one-day itinerary."
  heroMeta={[
    { label: 'From', value: `$${naivashaSix} per person, fees included` },
    { label: 'Departs', value: 'Daily, early morning' },
    { label: 'Returns', value: 'Same evening to Nairobi' },
  ]}
  itinerary={itinerary}
  included={included}
  notIncluded={notIncluded}
  costFactors={costFactors}
  faqs={faqs}
  photo="lake-naivasha"
  priceKeys={['naivashaHellsGate', 'lakeNakuru', 'amboseli']}
  priceNote="Mount Longonot and the Ngong Hills run on the same basis and quote lower, because their entry fees are smaller and the driving is shorter."
  ctaTitle="Pick a destination and we will tell you if the day works"
  ctaBody="Send the date you have free and where you want to go. If a destination is too far to enjoy in one day, we say so and suggest a better use of the same hours."
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p class="border-l-2 border-marigold pl-5 text-[length:var(--text-lede)] leading-relaxed text-ink">
      For two travellers, Lake Naivasha with Hell&rsquo;s Gate costs <strong>${naivashaTwo} per person</strong>,
      Lake Nakuru <strong>${nakuruTwo}</strong> and Amboseli <strong>${amboseliTwo}</strong>, park and activity fees
      included. Every price falls as the group grows, because the vehicle is shared.
    </p>

    <h2>Where a single day from Nairobi can genuinely reach</h2>
    <p>
      Nairobi sits at the edge of the Great Rift Valley, so several of Kenya&rsquo;s best-known landscapes are within
      a morning&rsquo;s drive. The escarpment viewpoint on the old Nairobi to Naivasha road is about an hour out of
      the city, Lake Naivasha and Hell&rsquo;s Gate are roughly 90 to 100 km away, Lake Nakuru National Park is
      around 160 km, and Amboseli National Park is around 240 km on the Mombasa road.
    </p>
    <p>
      Those distances decide the shape of the day. A Naivasha or Hell&rsquo;s Gate trip leaves time for two
      activities and an unhurried lunch. A Nakuru trip is a long day with a solid game drive in the middle. An
      Amboseli day is possible but heavy on driving, which is why we will tell you when an overnight is the better
      answer rather than sell you the longer version.
    </p>
    <h2>The destinations we drive most often</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Lake Naivasha</strong> for a boat ride among hippos and a walking safari on Crescent Island, where you walk among zebra and giraffe on foot.</li>
      <li><strong>Hell&rsquo;s Gate National Park</strong> for cycling between the rock towers and walking the gorge, one of the few Kenyan parks you can explore without a vehicle.</li>
      <li><strong>Lake Nakuru National Park</strong> for rhino, Rothschild&rsquo;s giraffe, lion and the birdlife of an alkaline Rift Valley lake.</li>
      <li><strong>Mount Longonot</strong> for the crater rim hike, a hard half-day climb with a view down into a volcanic crater forest.</li>
      <li><strong>The Ngong Hills</strong> for a ridge walk on Nairobi&rsquo;s doorstep, with the Rift Valley on one side and the city on the other.</li>
      <li><strong>Amboseli National Park</strong> for large elephant herds and, when the cloud lifts, Kilimanjaro behind them.</li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="body">
    <h2>Why we start these days early</h2>
    <p>
      Every hour of a day trip is spent either driving or doing the thing you came for, so the departure time
      directly buys activity time. Leaving Nairobi before the morning peak avoids the slow crawl out of the city,
      and arriving at a park gate early puts you in the best light for wildlife. Late starts do not simply shift the
      day, they shorten it at both ends.
    </p>
    <h2>Seasons and what they change</h2>
    <p>
      Kenya&rsquo;s long rains fall around March to May and the short rains around November to December, and the
      months between are drier. Rain affects day trips in specific ways rather than generally: gorge walking in
      Hell&rsquo;s Gate is restricted when flash flooding is a risk, park tracks at Nakuru and Amboseli soften, and
      the escarpment road slows in heavy downpours. Green season also delivers dramatic skies, fewer vehicles and
      strong birdlife, so we plan around the weather rather than avoid the season.
    </p>
    <h2>If you only have one day</h2>
    <p>
      Choose a destination by what you want the day to feel like. For maximum wildlife with minimum driving, the{' '}
      <a href="/tours/nairobi-national-park-game-drive/">Nairobi National Park game drive</a> is the strongest
      option. For a change of landscape and a boat on the water, Lake Naivasha. For something active on your own
      legs, Hell&rsquo;s Gate or Mount Longonot. Tell us your priority and we will make the recommendation before
      you commit.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</TourPageLayout>
